From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 17:17:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: separate WED and software token ranges

WED allocates its hardware TX buffers with token IDs starting at zero.
The software TX path currently allocates from the same range when WED uses
all 16384 hardware tokens.  On MT7990 this makes WED consume completions
for software-owned data tokens: TX-free events stop, the software token
count grows, and the AP eventually stalls.

Use the disjoint layout from MediaTek's current mt7996 implementation.
Reserve IDs 0..16383 for WED and allocate software tokens from
16384..31743.  The highest 1024 values remain unused, including 0x7fff,
which the TX-free format reserves as the invalid MSDU ID.

Keep the software pool available when flow offload is enabled.  Limiting
it to wed->wlan.token_start was appropriate when software occupied the
range below WED, but that boundary is now the start of the software range.

This extracts the token-layout portion of MediaTek's mt7996 token-size
refactor and adapts it to the current upstream driver and WED checks.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0054-mtk-mt76-add-debug-tools.patch
Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mmio.c   | 6 ++++--
 mt7996/mt7996.h | 2 +-
 wed.c           | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mmio.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -679,7 +679,7 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_d
 	}
 
 	wed->wlan.nbuf = tx_token_size;
-	wed->wlan.token_start = MT7996_TOKEN_SIZE - wed->wlan.nbuf;
+	wed->wlan.token_start = 0;
 	wed->wlan.hif2 = hif2;
 
 	wed->wlan.amsdu_max_subframes = 8;
@@ -703,6 +703,8 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_d
 		dev->mt76.rx_token_size = tx_token_size + rx_token_size;
 	}
 
+	dev->mt76.token_start = wed->wlan.nbuf;
+
 	*irq = wed->irq;
 	dev->mt76.dma_dev = wed->dev;
 
@@ -915,7 +917,7 @@ struct mt7996_dev *mt7996_mmio_probe(str
 		.survey_flags = SURVEY_INFO_TIME_TX |
 				SURVEY_INFO_TIME_RX |
 				SURVEY_INFO_TIME_BSS_RX,
-		.token_size = MT7996_TOKEN_SIZE,
+		.token_size = MT7996_SW_TOKEN_SIZE,
 		.tx_prepare_skb = mt7996_tx_prepare_skb,
 		.tx_complete_skb = mt76_connac_tx_complete_skb,
 		.rx_skb = mt7996_queue_rx_skb,
Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mt7996.h
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/mt7996.h
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mt7996.h
@@ -92,9 +92,9 @@
 #define MT7996_EEPROM_SIZE		7680
 #define MT7996_EEPROM_BLOCK_SIZE	16
 #define MT7996_EXT_EEPROM_BLOCK_SIZE	1024
-#define MT7996_TOKEN_SIZE		16384
 #define MT7996_HW_TOKEN_SIZE		8192
 #define MT7996_WED_TOKEN_SIZE		16384
+#define MT7996_SW_TOKEN_SIZE		15360
 
 #define MT7996_CFEND_RATE_DEFAULT	0x49	/* OFDM 24M */
 #define MT7996_CFEND_RATE_11B		0x03	/* 11B LP, 11M */
Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/wed.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/wed.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/wed.c
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ int mt76_wed_offload_enable(struct mtk_w
 	struct mt76_dev *dev = mt76_wed_to_dev(wed);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
-	dev->token_size = wed->wlan.token_start;
+	dev->token_size = dev->drv->token_size;
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
 
 	return !wait_event_timeout(dev->tx_wait, !dev->wed_token_count, HZ);
